From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Harris <wfh@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:12:32 -0700
Subject: Validate accessor callability in V8ObjectToPropertyDescriptor

V8ObjectToPropertyDescriptor previously omitted checking whether present
get and set attributes are callable or undefined per ECMA-262
ToPropertyDescriptor (steps 12.b and 14.b). During reentrant descriptor
conversion in the ObservableArray defineProperty trap, non-callable
values could be passed to v8::PropertyDescriptor and installed as an
AccessorPair, causing type confusion in V8.

Enforce that present getter and setter properties are either undefined
or callable functions, throwing a TypeError otherwise.

Bug: 557523002
Change-Id: Ia524d3c71cb5bb6085ef1d2bc0af650b55a87e9c
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8405731
Reviewed-by: Nate Chapin <japhet@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Will Harris <wfh@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698665}

